<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo eases on mark, eyes on central bank.</title>
<headline>Escudo eases on mark, eyes on central bank.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo slipped against the mark in early trade, reaching 100.59/60 to the German currency, and the Bank of Portugal might not want to see it go much lower, traders said.</p>
<p>The currency closed at 100.56/59 on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders said the escudo was being depressed by the weaker dollar and there were no local factors at work.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
